## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **TypeScript Migration:** The plan migrates from plain JS to TypeScript for type safety across agent boundaries. This means all existing `.js` files will be rewritten as `.ts`. The existing v1 code will remain functional during migration (we build v2 alongside, not destructively).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **New Dependencies:** This plan introduces PostgreSQL (via SQLite initially for simplicity), BullMQ (via an in-process queue initially), and optionally Neo4j. The initial implementation uses **lightweight alternatives** (SQLite + in-memory queue + adjacency-list graph) to avoid heavy infrastructure, with migration paths to full-scale services later.

> [!WARNING]
> **Breaking Change — Memory Schema:** v2 adds new fields to memory objects (`superseded_by`, `supersedes`, `graph_node_id`, `risk_level`, `task_ids`). Old `memory.jsonl` entries will be auto-migrated with a migration script, but the new schema is not backward-compatible with v1 consumers.

