#### [NEW] `src/v2/agents/observation-agent.ts`
**Refactors v1's** [watcher.js](file:///c:/Users/kolte/OneDrive/Desktop/all%20dev%20stuff/proj101/src/watcher.js) + [idempotency.js](file:///c:/Users/kolte/OneDrive/Desktop/all%20dev%20stuff/proj101/src/idempotency.js)

Responsibilities:
- Watches filesystem (Chokidar — same as v1)
- Watches git changes (new — `git log --oneline` polling or `git diff`)
- Normalizes all inputs into `ObservationEvent`:
  ```typescript
  interface ObservationEvent {
    type: 'file_added' | 'file_changed' | 'git_commit' | 'chat_log';
    filePath: string;
    content: string;
    diff?: string;
    metadata: {
      size: number;
      modifiedAt: string;
      gitCommitHash?: string;
    };
  }
  ```
- Idempotency check (same SHA-256 logic from v1)
- Emits `observation.new` events to the bus

**Key difference from v1:** The observation agent does NOT call the LLM. It only normalizes raw input. The summarizer logic moves to the Memory Extraction Agent.

